### Authentication flow
# Install "REST Client" (humao.rest-client) if you haven't.
# Click "Send Request" above any block to fire it.

@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Log in as admin
# Copy the accessToken from the response into the @accessToken variable
# at the top of orders.http and admin.http.
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
content-type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@laundry.local",
  "password": "changeme"
}

### 2. Extract tokens from the login response above
# You can reference {{login.response.body.accessToken}} in other requests
# if they live in this file. For cross-file use, copy/paste into @accessToken.
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 3. Who am I? (verifies the access token works)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/me
authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Refresh (rotates the refresh token)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/refresh
content-type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 5. Logout — bumps tokenVersion, invalidating all outstanding refresh tokens
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
